<section id="sec-intro" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>3-4-5 Triangle Calculator</h2>
  <p>Scale a 3-4-5 triangle and find its sides, area, and perimeter.</p>
  <p>A 3-4-5 triangle is a right triangle whose side lengths follow the ratio <span set:html={rich('[[3 : 4 : 5]]')} />. It is the most famous Pythagorean triple, because its whole-number sides satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: <span set:html={rich('[[3^2 + 4^2 = 5^2]]')} />, since <span set:html={rich('[[9 + 16 = 25]]')} />. The side of length 5 is the hypotenuse, and the sides of length 3 and 4 are the legs.</p>
  <p>The calculator scales that triangle by a positive scale factor <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} />, so the scaled sides are <span set:html={rich('[[a = 3k]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b = 4k]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[c = 5k]]')} />. It also works out the area, <span set:html={rich('[[A = 6k^2]]')} />, and the perimeter, <span set:html={rich('[[P = 12k]]')} />, so one input gives all five results. Use the <a href="/right-triangle-calculator/">right triangle calculator</a> for a general right triangle.</p>
  <p>For example, with <span set:html={rich('[[k = 2]]')} /> the sides become <span set:html={rich('[[a = 6]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b = 8]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[c = 10]]')} />, the area is <span set:html={rich('[[A = 24]]')} /> square units, and the perimeter is <span set:html={rich('[[P = 24]]')} /> units.</p>
</section>

