  <p>The calculator has a single mode: scale a 3-4-5 triangle. Enter a positive scale factor <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> and click Calculate, and it returns the three scaled side lengths, the area, and the perimeter. The table below lists each measurement with its formula.</p>
  <p>The scale factor <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> multiplies every original side. With <span set:html={rich('[[k = 1]]')} /> you get the original 3-4-5 triangle. A value above 1 enlarges it, and a value between 0 and 1 shrinks it. The calculator asks for <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> because the ratio fixes the shape: once <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> is known, every measurement follows.</p>
  <p>Enter a positive number only. If <span set:html={rich('[[k = 0]]')} />, all three sides become zero, which is a degenerate figure rather than a triangle, and a negative <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} /> cannot give valid side lengths. After calculating, use Reset to clear the field before starting a new problem.</p>
