  </ol>
  <p>The new triangle keeps the original 3:4:5 proportions: 6, 8, and 10 are all twice 3, 4, and 5. Check the right angle with Pythagoras: <span set:html={rich('[[6^2 + 8^2 = 36 + 64 = 100 = 10^2]]')} />. The area and the perimeter happen to share the number 24 here, but they measure different things.</p>
